 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? It depends how fluent you are in the language. If it' one of the tougher ones, like Arabic or Japanese, then the easy ones are great for travel. They use a lot of simple words and basic grammar, perfect for people who aren't regular readers. You find yourself understanding more than you'd expect. Most Dutch and Norwegian words sound easy to us, so the locals' voices are lovely to listen to. Netherlands has way more, per capita. They love their TV series there. Then enjoy the easier language. Get watching their versions of Game Shows. They' usually hilarious.",
